<%= header_section(@subject) %>
<div>
  <p>Hi there. We tried to send you <%= @amount %> through PayPal, but <%= @reason %>.</p>
  <% if @retries_stopped %>
    <p>
      <% if @no_payout_rail_available %>
        <%# Same rejection, but "until you change how you get paid" presumes a change they can make. %>
        We've stopped retrying this payout, because every attempt to that account will be refused. Your balance is safe and stays on your account.
      <% else %>
        This will keep happening until you change how you get paid, so we've stopped retrying it. Your balance is safe and stays on your account.
      <% end %>
    </p>
  <% elsif @retries_paused_by_pause %>
    <p>
      Payouts on your account are paused right now, so we'll only start trying again once they resume — and every attempt will fail until this is fixed. Your balance is safe and stays on your account.
    </p>
  <% else %>
    <p>
      We'll keep trying on your usual payout schedule, but every attempt will fail until this is fixed. Your balance is safe and stays on your account.
    </p>
  <% end %>
  <% if @no_payout_rail_available %>
    <p>
      <%# The cohort splits and we cannot tell the halves apart: some hold a usable PayPal account
          elsewhere, some cannot get one. Offer the first as a condition, answer the second plainly. %>
      PayPal will not send payments to accounts registered in that country, and bank transfer is not available in yours.
      If you have a PayPal account registered in a country PayPal does pay to, you can
      <a href='<%= settings_payments_url %>'>add it in your payout settings</a>.
      If you do not, we have no way to pay you right now.
    </p>
  <% elsif @can_receive_us_dollars_on_same_account %>
    <p>
      You can fix this on the PayPal account you already use: sign in to PayPal and add US dollars as a currency you accept.
      <% if @can_use_bank_account %>
        You can also <a href='<%= settings_payments_url %>'>add a bank account in your payout settings</a>, or switch to a different PayPal account that can receive US dollars.
      <% else %>
        Or <a href='<%= settings_payments_url %>'>use a different PayPal account</a> that can receive US dollars.
      <% end %>
    </p>
  <% elsif @locked_paypal_account %>
    <p>
      <%# Only PayPal can unlock the account, so the first step is always PayPal — never our
          settings, and never a differently-registered account, since the country did not fail. %>
      Sign in to PayPal to see whether there are restrictions on your account, or contact PayPal to have them lifted.
      <% if @can_use_bank_account %>
        You can also <a href='<%= settings_payments_url %>'>add a bank account in your payout settings</a>, or use a different PayPal account.
      <% else %>
        <%# The gumroad-private#1661 dead end: no bank rail, and telling them to find another PayPal
            account is an instruction much of this cohort has no way to follow. Say so plainly. %>
        PayPal is the only payout method we can offer in your country, so if PayPal cannot restore your account and you do not have
        <a href='<%= settings_payments_url %>'>another one to use</a>, we have no way to pay you right now. We hope to have a way to pay out your balance in the future.
      <% end %>
    </p>
  <% elsif @can_use_bank_account %>
    <p>
      <%# Reached only for the rejection that also takes the address off the account, so the copy
          says so rather than sending them to change something that is no longer there — except for
          a seller paid through a connected PayPal account, where there was no saved address to
          remove. An account in the same country would be refused the same way, so the alternative
          is described by country, not by currency. %>
      <% if @payout_address_removed %>
        We've removed that PayPal account from your payout settings, since we can't pay to it. To get paid,
        <a href='<%= settings_payments_url %>'>add a bank account there</a> instead, or a PayPal account registered in a country that can receive PayPal payments.
      <% else %>
        To get paid, <a href='<%= settings_payments_url %>'>add a bank account in your payout settings</a>, or connect a PayPal account registered in a country that can receive PayPal payments.
      <% end %>
    </p>
  <% else %>
    <p>
      <% if @payout_address_removed %>
        We've removed that PayPal account from your payout settings, since we can't pay to it. PayPal is the only payout method we can offer in your country, so to get paid you'll need to
        <a href='<%= settings_payments_url %>'>add a PayPal account</a> registered in a country that can receive PayPal payments.
      <% else %>
        PayPal is the only payout method we can offer in your country, so to get paid you'll need to
        <a href='<%= settings_payments_url %>'>connect a PayPal account</a> registered in a country that can receive PayPal payments.
      <% end %>
    </p>
  <% end %>
  <% if @payouts_on_hold && @payouts_paused_by_seller %>
    <p>
      <%# Both pauses are on. Naming only the hold would leave them waiting on us while their own
          toggle is still stopping the money. %>
      <% if @retries_paused_by_pause %>
        Two separate pauses are on your account: a hold on our side, which is ours to lift, and your own pause in your payout settings. Once a working payout method is on file,
      <% else %>
        Payouts on your account are also on hold on our side, and paused in your own payout settings. Once a working payout method is on file,
      <% end %>
      <a href='<%= settings_payments_url %>'>resume payouts in your settings</a> and reply to this email so we can review the hold and release your balance.
    </p>
  <% elsif @payouts_on_hold %>
    <p>
      <%# The pause is already named above when it is what stopped the retries, so don't restate it. %>
      <% if @retries_paused_by_pause %>
        That hold is ours to lift: once a working payout method is on file, reply to this email and we'll review the hold and release your balance.
      <% else %>
        Payouts on your account are also on hold. Once a working payout method is on file, reply to this email and we'll review the hold and release your balance.
      <% end %>
    </p>
  <% elsif @payouts_paused_by_seller %>
    <p>
      <% if @retries_paused_by_pause %>
        You paused them yourself, so once a working payout method is on file and you
      <% else %>
        Payouts on your account are also paused in your settings. Once a working payout method is on file and you
      <% end %>
      <a href='<%= settings_payments_url %>'>resume payouts there</a>, your balance will be sent on the next payout date.
    </p>
  <% elsif !@no_payout_rail_available %>
    <%# Withheld only here: with no rail and no pause, "on the next payout date after that" would
        date a payout against a change the seller may have no way to make. %>
    <p>
      Your balance will be sent on the next payout date after that.
    </p>
  <% end %>
</div>
